upernatural Tolerance exceeds your rating in IS requires 1 Ichor + 1 willpower point. Unlike the Vampire version, you use your effective Strength, rather than your permanent one. So, if you have Strength 4, IS 4 and Ravenous Hulk, you roll 4 + 4 + 2 = 10 dice. The 4 dot version of this Merit gives you 8 Again on the activation roll. [I don't think the Seductive and Competitive Beasts really fit the Symbiotes]<br /> <br /> <b>Hide Visage (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): </b>You gain the ability to hide not just from the five senses of mortals, but also from technology like thermal imaging. You gain 9 Again on Stealth rolls, which stacks with the dice bonus of the 3 dot version. You may also hide from supernatural senses for the scene by spending 1 Ichor point, using a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Venomous Projectile (\u25cf or \u25cf\u25cf): </b>By spending 1 Ichor, you can throw small poisonous barbs from your hands as an instant action, using Dexterity + Athletics - Defense. The 1 dot version and 2 dot versions inflict the moderate and grave Poisoned Tilt, respectively. The maximum range is [Stamina x 10] yards. The barbs only cause 1 bashing damage, which is enough to alert the target about your presence if you're firing from an obvious spot.<br /> <br /> <b>Thick Hide (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): </b>You have 2/2 Armor at all times, even if you are using Hide Visage. This stacks with the Iron Skin Merit and mundane Armor. By spending 1 Ichor, you can increase this to 4/4, but the Symbiote must be manifested and you must pay this cost for each attack received this turn. Attacks made with your Banes bypass this Armor.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some good suggestions. I'm not sure about the requirement to eat other Symbiotes, but other than that, they all seem like good things to include.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T16:56:39-07:00","id":880580,"title":"","content":"I'd be wary of adding that to the merit; otherwise, you take one dot of Ichorous Symbiote, and you get:<br /> \u2022 +1 HL.<br /> \u2022 +1 to an Attribute.<br /> \u2022 +1 to the Attribute Cap for your Physical Attributes.<br /> \u2022 2 dots of other merits.<br /> \u2022 <i>Much</i> faster healing.<br /> \u2022 A supernatural tolerance trait of 1.<br /> \u2022 +0L natural weapons.<br /> <br /> For <i>no</i> drawback other than the one you signed up for (you can reduce the &quot;oh noes, other symbiotes want to eat me&quot; by taking Small-Framed.)<br /> <br /> I'd pay an XP for that in a <i>hearbeat.</i> <hr /><br /> Keep in mind that the spoiled minor templates from Hurt Locker tend to get <i>very little</i> from the core merit, and usually have to deal with a harsh cost to use their other &quot;template&quot; powers.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Infected add their dots in Carrier to their pool to infect people with their disease; everything else revolves around their Conditions, which are both situational and <i>harsh</i>.<br /> \u2022 The Dreamers only get something really cool at the 5th dot of Subliminal Conditioning; everything below that can be reduced to &quot;Spend Memory to make better trick/called shots or get benefits of Trained Observer \u2022 for one roll. Get Memory from Breaking Points.&quot;<br /> \u2022 The Plain have <i>all violence ever</i> become a Breaking Point.<br /> \u2022 The Lost Boys actually take <i>more penalties</i> for each dot of The Protocol they take, and get no direct benefits.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that, as it stands, Ichorous Symbiot is <i>too good</i>. Or maybe Ichor is too good; the mortal &quot;exchange rate&quot; for healing is 1:2:6 for Bashing:Lethal:Aggravated, and that's <i>only</i> with Laying on Hands, which is (in my opinion) the best direct healing a mortal or mortal+ should have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:10:05-07:00","id":880588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879911-ichorous-symbiote-homebrew-mini-template?p=880580#post880580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be wary of adding that to the merit; otherwise, you take one dot of Ichorous Symbiote, and you get:<br /> \u2022 +1 HL.<br /> \u2022 +1 to an Attribute.<br /> \u2022 +1 to the Attribute Cap for your Physical Attributes.<br /> \u2022 2 dots of other merits.<br /> \u2022 <i>Much</i> faster healing.<br /> \u2022 A supernatural tolerance trait of 1.<br /> \u2022 +0L natural weapons.<br /> <br /> For <i>no</i> drawback other than the one you signed up for (you can reduce the &quot;oh noes, other symbiotes want to eat me&quot; by taking Small-Framed.)<br /> <br /> I'd pay an XP for that in a <i>hearbeat.</i> <hr /><br /> Keep in mind that the spoiled minor templates from Hurt Locker tend to get <i>very little</i> from the core merit, and usually have to deal with a harsh cost to use their other &quot;template&quot; powers.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Infected add their dots in Carrier to their pool to infect people with their disease; everything else revolves around their Conditions, which are both situational and <i>harsh</i>.<br /> \u2022 The Dreamers only get something really cool at the 5th dot of Subliminal Conditioning; everything below that can be reduced to &quot;Spend Memory to make better trick/called shots or get benefits of Trained Observer \u2022 for one roll. Get Memory from Breaking Points.&quot;<br /> \u2022 The Plain have <i>all violence ever</i> become a Breaking Point.<br /> \u2022 The Lost Boys actually take <i>more penalties</i> for each dot of The Protocol they take, and get no direct benefits.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that, as it stands, Ichorous Symbiot is <i>too good</i>. Or maybe Ichor is too good; the mortal &quot;exchange rate&quot; for healing is 1:2:6 for Bashing:Lethal:Aggravated, and that's <i>only</i> with Laying on Hands, which is (in my opinion) the best direct healing a mortal or mortal+ should have access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. I've toned back the core benefits, cutting the physical pool bonus and regeneration into Symbiotic Intensity and Mend Flesh respectively. I've also made the full regeneration cost 5 dots, and require 5 dots in the core merit, making the versiona accessible from 1 dot toned much further back.","signature":"<hr 